  "market_context": "Uptrend on GER40 1-hour chart, with price making higher highs and higher lows. The hidden bullish divergence formed after a break of structure, during a pullback into the discount zone of a Gann box (PD array).",
  "key_observation": "Price made a higher low while RSI made a lower low during an uptrend, forming a hidden bullish divergence—indicating trend continuation—located in the discount (lower half) zone of the PD array.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified the uptrend via market structure (higher highs and higher lows) and confirmed with a rising trend line.",
    "Step 2: Located two consecutive swing lows where price made a higher low but RSI made a lower low, confirming a hidden bullish divergence.",
    "Step 3: Drew a Gann box from the swing high to swing low of the impulse move that broke prior structure to define the PD array (premium/discount zones).",
    "Step 4: Observed that the divergence occurred within the lower half (discount zone) of the PD array, adding confluence for a long entry.",
    "Step 5: Set take-profit at the previous swing high (structure level), as the most probable target for trend continuation."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Hidden bullish divergences in uptrends are high-probability continuation signals—especially when they align with the discount zone of a PD array. Always confirm with market structure and use prior swing highs as TP1.",
